  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square marker painting of overlapping cartoon creatures with white horns, spots and visors in rainbow colours over black, with heavy black outlines.",
    "description": "A square marker painting on wood. The whole surface is cut into cells by thick black lines over a rainbow of green, cyan, pink, orange, yellow and purple fills. Creatures emerge from the cells: a purple and blue bird like head with a white beak at lower centre, a lime face with white antennae at upper left, orange spotted forms, white horns, visors, and dots. A blue and lilac creature with a hood at lower right. White highlight marks on every horn and beak.",
    "impression": "The crowd painting that is closest to a pure pattern, where the black grid matters more than any single face. It looks like a stained glass window designed by a child who loves monsters. Finding the creatures takes a moment, which is the pleasure.",
